{"event_type":"review","id":"70f0f7e2672274bfb918452b46545f3926d0ea4f9ee8378894f03c2d9a3efef3","occurred_at":"2026-11-12T01:34:59Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9399bf37ee4a25b5c67584a0106dad1517e2c3b09b4f94a0eefc833370f1af59","sha256":"9399bf37ee4a25b5c67584a0106dad1517e2c3b09b4f94a0eefc833370f1af59"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e7fdf7dfd3a45c2aa621a77947bc9c0ac8dfab4bc5545039cb12c583738f9b5e","sha256":"e7fdf7dfd3a45c2aa621a77947bc9c0ac8dfab4bc5545039cb12c583738f9b5e"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b37f7244a2ccb6fca6bedb0b6b4bbc0c5829132f02b1e3acc59c5722fcefe65b","sha256":"b37f7244a2ccb6fca6bedb0b6b4bbc0c5829132f02b1e3acc59c5722fcefe65b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/76974a93a14af9597a407225525810aeda975f990ddb4a02aea78b63e752a303","sha256":"76974a93a14af9597a407225525810aeda975f990ddb4a02aea78b63e752a303"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/055de29b986f29b0512371e8e420d4ffde9235ca65cc371ed96e1708fc82fe30","sha256":"055de29b986f29b0512371e8e420d4ffde9235ca65cc371ed96e1708fc82fe30"}],"attempt_id":"f8d730a9b3006a5dd633a5689130e50b3f142ba81587eaa7f50d2eb47fc5895b:0:1","base":"47e6c5c9091bec406571b580dfcaf6b8bf0736a0","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"a34f585ba8c8ce66c287f343625bb42b74df7f07","body":"**Reject an empty baseline instead of omitting baseline accounting.**\n\nIf `original` is `{}`, Line 96 skips the digest check. `summary()` then returns `baseline: None` rather than rejecting invalid evidence. It can also report `strict_T1_zero: True` for a currently empty T1 inventory without reporting the requested historical baseline debt. Validate every provided baseline.\n\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed change</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    if original:\n+    if original is not None:\n```\n</details>","id":"3606b7f1c7b7ab3849ad7993151df3ac631529266f40d6b78d0eb78820d63fa0","intervals":[[96,96]],"path":"apps/crq-python/backfill_report.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject an empty baseline instead of omitting baseline accounting."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"6f30b9dd4edde96c464765d1f3d0866f9334bd7e","body":"**Recalculate the remaining budget after retaining the previous attempt.**\n\n`remaining` is calculated before `retain()` and the Git reset commands on Lines 203–206. Those operations consume the same wall-clock budget, but the next provider receives the earlier value.\n\nFor example, with a 60-second budget, a rate limit at 45 seconds and 20 seconds of retention allow another provider to start after the deadline with 15 seconds remaining. Retention includes blocking Git calls (`apps/crq-python/crq_repair/retain.py:62-84`).\n\nRecalculate `remaining` after cleanup. Stop before `_dispatch()` if the deadline has expired.","id":"5c7bbb6656955078bf975efe0e5de2aa5b1d41336bb992bf473edde9f9c63f41","intervals":[[209,209]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Recalculate the remaining budget after retaining the previous attempt."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"b5bd7a030128518238348b810cc4e14804eb0003","body":"**Follow-up: retain feedback after an unverified GraphQL miss.**\n\nIf REST contains the source thread before GraphQL exposes it, `source_thread()` returns `None` (`apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py:691-709`). This line still records feedback as complete. Reconciliation then sets `fix_merged` and prevents another attempt.\n\nVerify absence through REST, or keep feedback pending. Carry the delayed-thread case as a named test.\n\nAs per coding guidelines, I11 requires “GraphQL reviewThreads lag REST (verify via REST).” Based on learnings, P2/Minor findings are deferred to follow-up issues.","id":"1191e204c7a9a0cbdf93028d59d54e08d30e51e6f943136c0e8964686b187d9b","intervals":[[741,741]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Follow-up: retain feedback after an unverified GraphQL miss."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"b5bd7a030128518238348b810cc4e14804eb0003","body":"**Scan every logical line in the fix instructions.**\n\nIf instructions contain a lone `\\r` or `\\u0085`, this split leaves the following text without a patch prefix. However, `secret_scan_diff()` uses `splitlines()` and skips fragments without `+` or `-` (`apps/crq-python/crq.py:436-452`). A denylist match after that separator therefore escapes inspection. The optional gitleaks pass does not replace repository-specific denylist rules.\n\nBuild the scan representation with the same line boundaries as the scanner. Preserve the original instructions separately in the job.","id":"8bc5f9a7ae02e0434cd669ff3c37be8070778ab045e54de06f0d03649d2ec223","intervals":[[23,23]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Scan every logical line in the fix instructions."}],"head":"7e4f4073122589cb7d4d00a079e6dc98f0291f35","head_tree":"1ecd116c4ac33bbae984033dfd03894947e6454f","input_scope":[{"blob":"a34f585ba8c8ce66c287f343625bb42b74df7f07","intervals":[[1,160]],"path":"apps/crq-python/backfill_report.py"},{"blob":"6f30b9dd4edde96c464765d1f3d0866f9334bd7e","intervals":[[1,858]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py"},{"blob":"b5bd7a030128518238348b810cc4e14804eb0003","intervals":[[1,936]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py"},{"blob":"cd8d2e81a297c94fa8858d64c04ba1aee650d6c6","intervals":[[1,175]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_backfill_report.py"},{"blob":"3f004c072e5336ddbe050ebd8504152db246313f","intervals":[[1,347]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_deploy_controller_unit_switch.py"},{"blob":"d9eddcdd2917d917eaf3d0d260dbb8a15013eca1","intervals":[[1,459